# Z-UI dogfooding

Before adding UI (controls, layout chrome, dividers, copy actions, feedback, overlays, or docs chrome), **search the library first**. Prefer shipping with `@z-ux/ui` and semantic CSS variables over custom markup or one-off styles.

## Checklist (do this before inventing)

1. **Components** — Search `packages/react/src/components/` and `@z-ux/ui` / `@z-ux/ui/<name>` exports. Use an existing component when it fits (e.g. `Button`, `IconButton`, `Card`, `Separator`, `Badge`, `Field`, `Stack`, `Spinner`, `Tooltip`).
2. **Tokens** — Style with semantic variables (`--z-color-*`, `--z-spacing-*`, `--z-text-*`, `--z-radius-*`, `--z-motion-*`, `--z-elevation-*`). Confirm role in the matching `*-SEMANTICS.md` and root CSS (`colors.css`, `sizes.css`, `text.css`, `motion.css`, `elevation.css`). Never hardcode colors, rem sizes, or easings when a semantic token exists.
3. **Compose, don’t fork** — Build from library primitives + tokens. Do not recreate dividers with `border-top`, buttons with raw `<button>` + custom CSS, or cards with ad-hoc boxes when `Separator`, `Button`/`IconButton`, or `Card` exist.
4. **Gaps** — If nothing fits, say so and ask before adding a new component, semantic token, or documented exception. Do not paper over gaps with primitives or one-off CSS.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — invent a divider
<div style={{ borderTop: '1px solid #eee', marginTop: 8 }} />

// ✅ GOOD — library + semantic stack
<Separator className="docs-token-card__separator" />
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.meta { margin-block: 0.5rem; color: #666; }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.meta { margin-block: var(--z-spacing-stack-component); color: var(--z-color-text-secondary); }
```

## Scope notes

- Applies to apps (`apps/docs`, `apps/preview`), examples, and any consumer UI in this repo.
- When **editing** a component under `packages/react/src/components/**`, also follow `z-ui-component-standards` and the component-editing skill.
- Token source of truth remains `z-ui-token-sources` — never edit `dist/**` by hand.
